      "note": [
        "For the quarter three 2023, a correction of reported errors has been performed regarding financial derivates. This affects the item 3.3 Financial derivates within the balance of payments. In connection with the publication of 2023Q3, the previous reported errors have been corrected for 2023Q2.  As a result of the changes, there will be a time series break between 2023Q1 and 2023Q2. Statistics Sweden will address this break in future publications. ",
        "In connection with the publication of first quarter 2024, information regarding account item 3.3 financial derivatives has been revised from first quarter 2013 up to and including first quarter 2023. The revision is based on model estimates and involves a certain degree of uncertainty. The new data is judged to be of higher quality than previously published series.",
        "Reinvested earnings within direct investments has been adjusted for the reference period of first quarter of 2013 to the fourth quarter of 2022. The adjustment aims to better reflect the income measurement Net Operating Surplus (NOS).",
        "Correction 2026-09-18: In the publication released on 2026-09-04, incorrect data were included regarding long-term debt securities issued by the Central bank in SEK. The error concerned an incorrect registration that resulted in a non existent holding abroad. The correction affects only the data for the second quarter of 2026, and the stock value and corresponding transaction have been adjusted from SEK 37 billion to zero. As of 2026 09 18, the error has been corrected, and the tables are now showing accurate figures.",
        "New sources have been used for the compilation of Sweden´s balance of payments for transactions in portfolio investments and for debt securities in the reserve assets from the first quarter of 2019. This affects the comparison with previous periods. For further information, see the document New data sources for statistics on securities under More information."
      ],
